# Optional build configuration for Tempo source builds.
# Tempo has no hosted service of its own. With nothing set here, cloud features
# (T3 Connect sign-in and relay), telemetry and desktop updates stay off and
# their UI is hidden. Copy to `.env` and fill in only what you run yourself.
# Do not add server-side secrets to this file.

# Your own PostHog project. The server reads this from its environment when it
# starts; no build carries a key. Without it the server sends no telemetry.
# T3CODE_POSTHOG_KEY=phc_...

# Apple signing. Signed macOS builds stop with an error until T3CODE_APPLE_TEAM_ID names
# the 10-character Apple Developer Team ID that signs them; unsigned local builds need none.
# Signed macOS builds also need a Developer ID provisioning profile for local.tempo.app;
# without Clerk below they sign with no associated domains.
# T3CODE_APPLE_TEAM_ID=ABC1234567
# T3CODE_MACOS_PROVISIONING_PROFILE=/absolute/path/to/tempo.provisionprofile

# Desktop update feed. Builds have no update feed unless this names the GitHub
# repository whose releases the app should update from. A build that runs in
# GitHub Actions uses that run's GITHUB_REPOSITORY when this is unset.
# T3CODE_DESKTOP_UPDATE_REPOSITORY=owner/repo

# Cloud features (Clerk sign-in and the relay) stay off unless you name your own
# deployment here. Never point these at T3 Code's production values.
# T3CODE_CLERK_PUBLISHABLE_KEY=pk_...
# T3CODE_CLERK_JWT_TEMPLATE=...
# T3CODE_CLERK_CLI_OAUTH_CLIENT_ID=...
# T3CODE_RELAY_URL=https://relay.example.com
# T3CODE_HOSTED_APP_URL=https://app.example.com
